 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser tools
+
+The shared layout exposes WebMCP tools in browsers supporting
+[`document.modelContext`](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+Other browsers can use the same search and bookmark controls normally.
+
+- `open_search` opens the `search_articles` form. Its required `query` field
+  searches titles and summaries and returns matching article metadata and URLs.
+- `open_reading_list` displays saved articles and opens the `update_reading_list`
+  form. Choose an article `slug` and an `action` (`add` or `remove`). Repeating
+  the same action preserves the requested state. Changes update bookmark icons.
+- Article pages expose `get_tide_levels` (coastal-pulse), `get_coffee_brew`
+  (coffee-alchemy), `get_plant_stats` (silent-architects), or
+  `get_article_popularity` (super-bowl-lx). Each takes no arguments and returns
+  the HTTP status, final URL, redirect flag, and response body, or a network error.
+  Popularity requests use the current article's ID.
+
+Both [declarative forms](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api)
+return results using `SubmitEvent.respondWith` when invoked by an agent. Tool
+registrations are scoped to the current page and cleaned up during Astro client
+navigation. The article APIs intentionally simulate failures for DevTools
+exercises; these failures are returned to agents as well.
